// A container naming its own layout engine (DD-14 C1, C2): `box` is laid out
// by `grid` on its own and placed as one box by the document's engine (`grid`,
// in the pipeline harness, which honours the container engines it has, C46).
// A grid box in a grid document composes to the picture grid alone draws
// (C31), so its render goldens are those it had when the key was ignored. No
// diagnostic: `SGL4010`'s fixture is `unknown-key.sgl`, and an engine that is
// not available is `engine-unknown.sgl`'s `SGL4012`.
box: {
  @label: "Box"
  @layout: { engine: grid }
  a: "A"
  b: "B"
  a -> b
}
